- which exact owner/proof boundary must close each gap.

The central property is **status and authority separation**. Accepted Implementation is not Architecture authority. Implementation target text is not current source. Source presence is not execution. A passing package test is not a live Edge proof. Runtime observation is not Product support. Model or agent self-report is not conformance evidence. The handler may project and compare these layers, but it may not promote one into another.

This crate is stateless and candidate-only. It does not run source analysis, tests, binaries or providers; acquire evidence; edit Architecture/Implementation/source; create work units/issues/branches/PRs; mutate support state; grant authority; execute effects; or finish a task.

